{
  "units": [
    {
      "title": "Structured vs Unstructured Data",
      "source_segment_ids": ["REL_0001", "FCT_0022"],
      "mode": "text_and_visual",
      "remaining_text": "",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "source_segment_ids": ["REL_0001", "FCT_0022"],
          "needs_review": false,
          "missing_information": null,
          "evidence": [
            {
              "note_id": "REL_0001",
              "exact_quote": "Structured data (rows and columns) differs from unstructured data (images, text, video) which lack a tabular format and thus present challenges for machine‑learning models."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "FCT_0022",
              "exact_quote": "Algorithms such as DBSCAN, K-means, and hierarchical clustering are examples of unsupervised machine learning algorithms."
            }
          ],
          "payload": {
            "type": "table",
            "title": "Structured vs Unstructured Data",
            "headers": ["Aspect", "Structured Data", "Unstructured Data"],
            "rows": [
              ["Format", "Rows and columns (tabular)", "Images, text, video, audio"],
              ["Typical Algorithms", "Statistical ML (e.g., decision tree, XGBoost)", "Deep learning (CNNs, RNNs, Transformers)"],
              ["Challenges", "Requires feature engineering", "Requires large labeled datasets"]
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Statistical ML vs Deep Learning Guidance",
      "source_segment_ids": ["FCT_0024", "FCT_0025", "FCT_0026", "FCT_0028", "FCT_0030"],
      "mode": "text_and_visual",
      "remaining_text": "",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "source_segment_ids": ["FCT_0024", "FCT_0025", "FCT_0026", "FCT_0028", "FCT_0030"],
          "needs_review": false,
          "missing_information": null,
          "evidence": [
            {
              "note_id": "FCT_0024",
              "exact_quote": "If you have simple features, such as structured data in tables, you should use statistical machine learning."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "FCT_0025",
              "exact_quote": "If you have complex features, such as images, videos, or other unstructured data, you should use deep learning."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "FCT_0026",
              "exact_quote": "Deep learning can also be applied to structured data, even though it is not the default recommendation."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "FCT_0028",
              "exact_quote": "Choosing between statistical ML and deep learning requires using these loose guidelines and then experimenting to see which approach gives the best performance."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "FCT_0030",
              "exact_quote": "If you have a huge number of training samples, deep learning will usually perform better."
            }
          ],
          "payload": {
            "type": "table",
            "title": "When to Use Statistical ML vs Deep Learning",
            "headers": ["Criterion", "Statistical ML", "Deep Learning"],
            "rows": [
              ["Feature Type", "Simple, tabular features", "Complex, unstructured features (images, video, audio, text)"],
              ["Data Size", "Moderate", "Large (many training samples)"],
              ["Default Recommendation", "Use statistical ML", "Use deep learning (but can apply to structured data)"],
              ["Experimentation Needed", "Yes", "Yes"]
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Transformer Architecture Overview",
